ocId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"Known as fixed-size chunking, the traditional way to chunk is to cut documents into chunks of a fixed length such as 200 tokens (Gao et al., 2023)."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_40b5abbf99c43c4e","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":17,"quote":"Figure 7: Example of chunking a normal document using different chunkers."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_40b5abbf99c43c4e","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":17,"quote":"Figure 6: Example of chunking a stitched document using different chunkers."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_32b739461e661ec5","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":17,"quote":"F Combine EDC with other IE tools EDC can be integrated with other IE tools, in- cluding chunking, coreference, and entity de- duplication."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_40b5abbf99c43c4e","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":17,"quote":"Each subplot’s y-label indicates the fixed hyperparameter value, with n_sents_overlap increasing from top to bottom. Figure 6: Example of chunking a stitched document using different chunkers."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_f5edef1f89ea1d6d","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"ng and highlight the need for more efficient chunking strategies in RAG systems."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_181c8bf27b0b14b3","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":3,"quote":"4 Results 4.1 Measuring and reporting performances As mentioned earlier, we used three proxy tasks the study chunking. We cannot directly assess the quality of retrieval at the chunk level due to the lack of ground-truth at the chunk level."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_ac7298f01655cdf6","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"Despite its growing adoption, the actual benefits over sim- pler fixed-size chunking, where documents are split into consecutive, fixed-size segments, re- main unclear."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_ac7298f01655cdf6","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"These findings challenge the previous assumptions about semantic chunk- ing and highlight the need for more efficient chunking strategies in RAG systems."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_63b70d30e6c602f7","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":8,"quote":"1) Chunking Strategy: The most common method is to split the document into chunks on a fixed number of tokens (e.g., 100, 256, 512) [88]."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_ac7298f01655cdf6","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"Is Semantic Chunking Worth the Computational Cost?"},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_d65ed3f1803eadf1","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":27,"quote":"More work is needed to address this limitation since further chunking would only create other issues due to sentence interdependence."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_62e78ed097a9e5e1","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"Recently, there has been a surge of interest in semantic chunking, where documents are seg- mented based on semantic similarity, with some in- dustry applications suggesting promising improve- ments in performance (LangChain, 2024;"},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_1cf0759a18d52fa5","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":3,"quote":"Most documents on the BEIR benchmark (Thakur et al., 2021) are too short for chunking to be effective."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_267bb9040788f52b","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":4,"quote":"However, the performance differences between the Fixed-size Chunker and the two semantic chunkers were minimal, suggesting no clear advantage for any specific chunking strategy."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_c0c23ec7486789bd","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":11,"quote":"This showed that even with added positional information, semantic-based chunking could misgroup content that shared con- text, as these sentences were clearly about the sales of Interact Home Computer."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_cf1b7dfeca5d2412","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":4,"quote":"The impact of chunk- ing strategy was often overshadowed by other fac- tors, such as the quality of embeddings, especially when computational resources are limited or when working with standard document structures."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_60af1dfe86016485","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":8,"quote":"Financial report chunking for effective retrieval augmented generation."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_5ce0cc847e090e6c","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":8,"quote":"Ini- tially, we experimented with datasets from BEIR (Thakur et al., 2021), but the short length of these documents showed no performance improvement with chunking."},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_ff1229c3ff9df8c8","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"In general, our contributions are: • We present a novel, large-scale evaluation framework comparing semantic and fixed-size chunking across diverse tasks."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"bd72eebf611df136_c_39ff7dc4df4647e3","docId":"bd72eebf611df136","docTitle":"2410.05779_LightRAG_Simple_and_Fast_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":1,"quote":"By breaking down a large external text corpus into smaller, more manageable segments, chunking significantly enhances the accuracy of information retrieval."},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_81b89429614de17d","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":5,"quote":"Further exploration of con- textual embeddings is necessary before definitively concluding the limitations of semantic chunking."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_62e78ed097a9e5e1","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"Such a systematic evaluation is not trivial due to the lack of data that can be directly used to com- pare chunking strategies."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_8f9c822c2236bc29","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":5,"quote":"A dataset containing all these elements is needed for a more thorough evaluation of chunking strategies."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_7b79964ed96d7d7b","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":4,"quote":"Semantic chunking occasionally improved performance, particularly on stitched datasets with high topic diversity."},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_32b739461e661ec5","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":17,"quote":"We ran experiments on Re-DOCRED (Tan et al., 2022) by combining EDC with LingMess (Otmazgin et al., 2023), a SOTA coreference resolution method and simple sentence-level chunking."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_19d2c1fdea24971d","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":11,"quote":"These examples underscore that se- mantic similarity alone is not a reliable measure for effective chunking, and it may be less useful than straightforward positional information."},{"id":"c29","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_f5edef1f89ea1d6d","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"How- ever, the effectiveness of chunking strategies re- mains a significant challenge in optimizing retrieval quality and computational efficiency (Lewis et al., 2020; Finardi et al., 2024)."},{"id":"c30","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_88d531172afa0e68","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":3,"quote":"Some prior work proposes criteria for having LLMs quantify the quality of 3 Source Documents Text Chunks text extraction and chunking Entities & Relationships domain-tailored summarization Knowledge Graph domain-tailored summarization"},{"id":"c31","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_fb198057dee65e19","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":21,"quote":"This is done by chunking the textual and relational information of each entity, with each chunk being embedded into its own vector."},{"id":"c32","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_fcc8c0c3719c8c55","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":1,"quote":"For instance, traditional RAG systems often use paragraph-level chunking techniques, which assume the text in those documents are uniform in length."},{"id":"c33","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_d9d59e3b6e3174b5","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":5,"quote":"This chunking strategy employs a size of 2024 characters with an overlap of 204 characters, ensuring comprehensive coverage while maintaining context across segment boundaries."}],"mastery":null}},{"type":"NotesGraph","id":"notes-graph","meta":{"status":"ready","error":null},"data":{"focusId":"chunking","query":"","nodes":[{"id":"chunking","label":"chunking","kind":"method","passages":27,"documents":8,"degree":54,"mastery":null},{"id":"graph_based_retrieval_augmented_generation","label":"Self-Reflective Retrieval-Augmented Generation","kind":"method","passages":538,"documents":14,"degree":638,"mastery":0.6},{"id":"rag_system","label":"RAG systems","kind":"method","passages":64,"documents":9,"degree":73,"mastery":null},{"id":"fixed_size_chunking","label":"Fixed-size chunking","kind":"method","passages":7,"documents":1,"degree":13,"mastery":null},{"id":"retrieval","label":"retrieval","kind":"concept","passages":600,"documents":16,"degree":651,"mastery":0.206},{"id":"edc","label":"Extract, Define, Canonicalize","kind":"method","passages":46,"documents":1,"degree":89,"mastery":null},{"id":"stitched_document","label":"stitched documents","kind":"task","passages":7,"documents":1,"degree":9,"mastery":null},{"id":"n_sents_overlap","label":"n_sents_overlap","kind":"metric","passages":2,"documents":1,"degree":1,"mastery":null},{"id":"normal_document","lab